From ce0008a43af42881a83e84249dea7b5b03873a83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:58:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/50] Mfi: add native hardware plugin for Ubiquiti mFi/mPower

Polls the device's local JSON API over a cookie session and publishes, per
port, a kWh meter, an On/Off switch and a load-detection alert; THS probes get
a temperature sensor instead. Writes are read back to confirm.

The session cookie goes out as an explicit header rather than through the
process-wide cookie jar, so more than one device can be configured at once.

Two quirks of firmware 2.1, both confirmed against the vendor's own CGI
source. The API no longer carries an energy field, only per-calendar-month
counters, so the lifetime total is accumulated from month-to-month deltas and
handles the rollover. The enabled field is a driver-level flag that reads 0
even on a port drawing current, so load detection uses power and current
thresholds rather than trusting it.

Note the hardware's own energy counter reads zero on some units despite real
draw, which leaves the kWh total at zero through no fault of this code.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [WIP]
